                <pb facs="0552" n="408" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg408"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/635: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Yugoslavia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >George</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-07T12:00:00+01:00">December 7,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 6:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>23. Department’s circular of December 1, 4 p.m. I am orally informed by Foreign
                    Office, Yugoslav Minister at Washington telegraphically instructed to accomplish
                    full adherence to proposals regarding Manchuria and that declaration will be
                    published in Belgrade.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
